(?R), unanchored
  (a(b)c)    found '(a(b)c)'
  ((a)(b))   found '((a)(b))'
  ()         found '()'
  (a(b)c     found '(b)'
  a          no match

^...(?R)...$ -- the anchors are INSIDE the recursion
  (a(b)c)    no match
  ((a)(b))   no match
  ()         match
  (a(b)c     no match
  a          no match

^((?1) form)$ -- whole subject must be one balanced group
  (a(b)c)    match
  ((a)(b))   match
  ()         match
  (a(b)c     no match
  a          no match

^((?&par) form)$ -- the same thing, named
  (a(b)c)    match
  ((a)(b))   match
  ()         match
  (a(b)c     no match
  a          no match

subroutine call vs backreference
  12-34    (?1) yes  \1 no
  12-12    (?1) yes  \1 yes

nesting depth, with the (?1) form
  depth 1     match
  depth 10    match
  depth 100   match
  depth 1000  match
